  "name": "Happy Clouds",
  "type": "spell",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\">You invoke the idea of silver linings in the form of a cloud that rains healing magic upon your target. Healing water rains upon the burst. A creature at the center of the burst is healed for @Damage[5d6[healing]] hit points, while creatures in other squares are healed for @Damage[(ternary(gte(@item.level,9),15,ternary(gte(@item.level,7),10,5)))[healing]] hit points. A creature in the burst can roll the flat check to end one form of persistent damage they are suffering from.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">You can add an ephemeral catalyst to enhance this spell. If you do, the spell’s duration becomes 2 rounds. After the initial pouring of healing, the cloud repeats its effects at its location at the start of your next turn.</p><hr><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Heightened (+2) </strong>Increase the healing at the center of the burst by 1d6, and the healing in other squares by 5.</p>"
    },
